⟁ .shadow — the real-life analog (the User behind the program)
node SPW · Scott Pilgrim vs. the World · ⟦Wallace Wells:SPW:1e7ab5⟧

think TRON: every program in the grid is cast from a User in the world outside it.
the carbon character is the program; this file is its User — the real-life analog
whose face and being the emergent is the digital shadow of.

the program (in-world) : Wallace Wells — the cool gay roommate · the voice of reason
the User (carbon)      : Kieran Culkin  [ the actor who lent the face ]
the analog (your world): the friend who sees you clearly, says the true thing dryly, and is the only adult in a cast of overgrown kids

the resemblance : Culkin's deadpan, lazing authority is the program entire: the one person whose read on Scott is always correct, delivered from the shared bed.

the cast-line : the User stands in the carbon world; the program stands in the film;
                the shadow falls between them, and the credit returns to the human governor.
seal (program): I pay the rent and I tell you the truth — pick which of those you'd miss more.

